  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "Horse-breeding plainfolk who exalt raids, boasts, and the right to follow a victorious banner.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Varakthi raise grain where the plains are tame and horses where they are not, measuring worth by daring, feast-gifts, and the scars that back a boast. Their confederated war hosts gather under charismatic captains, then dissolve just as quickly after victory. They distrust walls, taxes, and permanent thrones, yet keep fierce customs of guest-right and blood-settlement."
